{"gene":"MYD88","uniprot":"Q99836","proteinName":"myeloid differentiation primary response protein MyD88 isoform 2","function":"Adapter protein involved in the Toll-like receptor and IL-1 receptor signaling pathway in the innate immune response. Acts via IRAK1, IRAK2, IRF7 and TRAF6, leading to NF-kappa-B activation, cytokine secretion and the inflammatory response. Increases IL-8 transcription. Involved in IL-18-mediated signaling pathway. Activates IRF1 resulting in its rapid migration into the nucleus to mediate an efficient induction of IFN-beta, NOS2/INOS, and IL12A genes. Upon TLR8 activation by GU-rich single-stranded RNA (GU-rich RNA) derived from viruses such as SARS-CoV-2, SARS-CoV and HIV-1, induces IL1B release through NLRP3 inflammasome activation. MyD88-mediated signaling in intestinal epithelial cells is crucial for maintenance of gut homeostasis and controls the expression of the antimicrobial lectin REG3G in the small intestine","pathwayComment":null,"pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-1280218","name":"Adaptive Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1236975","name":"Antigen processing-Cross presentation","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-983169","name":"Class I MHC mediated antigen processing & presentation","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1280215","name":"Cytokine Signaling in Immune system","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1834949","name":"Cytosolic sensors of pathogen-associated DNA ","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-73887","name":"Death Receptor Signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-3134963","name":"DEx/H-box helicases activate type I IFN and inflammatory cytokines production ","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-5602358","name":"Diseases associated with the TLR signaling cascade","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-5260271","name":"Diseases of Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top